The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (tag_exists(name))
    n->item = get_item_from_tag(name);
```
Reason:
The function did not properly check for the special case of the node name `"__root__"`. As a result, when the name was `"__root__"`, the function would incorrectly call `get_item_from_tag(name)`, which could lead to errors or incorrect behavior since it was not designed to handle the root node correctly.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!strcmp(name, "__root__"))
    n->item = list_first_entry_or_null(&menu.master, struct item, master);
else
    n->item = get_item_from_tag(name);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a specific check for the node name `"__root__"`, ensuring that when this name is encountered, the function retrieves the correct item for the root node from the `menu.master` list instead of incorrectly attempting to get it from tags. This ensures proper handling of the root node and prevents potential errors.

